  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration><qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Choose the word that best completes the sentence.</p><p>The professor's seminar covers the temples of Athens and the forums of Rome -- ____ in the strict sense, ending well before the fall of the Western empire.</p><qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1"><qti-simple-choice identifier="A">the Middle Ages</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">the Renaissance</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">antiquity</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">the Enlightenment</qti-simple-choice></qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="CORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Antiquity is the ancient Greco-Roman past, matching Athenian temples and Roman forums and ending before the fall of the Western empire.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="INCORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Antiquity is the precise fit because the seminar's material is Greek and Roman and stops before the Western empire falls. The Middle Ages begin only after that fall, so the final clause rules them out. The Renaissance is a much later revival of classical learning, and the Enlightenment is later still.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body><qti-response-processing><qti-response-condition><qti-response-if><qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-correct identifier="RESPONSE"/></qti-match><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value><qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">CORRECT</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
